MerkleAdapterCapabilities
├── constructor
│   └── stores zero and non-contract capability registries without validation
├── addCapability
│   ├── requires registry approval for the exact adapter and installation by its owner
│   ├── requires a nonempty whitelist for this adapter and capability
│   ├── rejects approvals scoped to another registry or adapter
│   ├── rejects unapproved modules, nonowners and duplicate installation
│   ├── rolls back every selector and enumeration entry on a selector collision
│   ├── registers and removes every compiler-emitted native selector
│   ├── preserves native reads, writes and authorization when their selectors are registered
│   └── registers and removes the proxy upgrade selector while preserving proxy authorization and dispatch
├── registry selector replacement
│   ├── leaves installed routes unchanged
│   ├── removal clears only the original local list
│   └── reinstallation uses the new list
├── removeCapability
│   ├── clears every selector while retaining unrelated capabilities
│   ├── rejects nonowners and missing or already removed modules
│   ├── remains available after registry approval is revoked
│   ├── remains available when the capabilities registry is unavailable
│   └── permits freed selectors to be reused while preserving namespaced adapter state
├── fallback
│   ├── preserves sender, value, adapter context and adapter ETH balance
│   ├── isolates namespaced state between adapters sharing one implementation
│   ├── leaves native ownership, roles, vault, oracle and accounting state intact
│   ├── supports an extension protocol callback under STATICCALL at the adapter address
│   ├── keeps installed static callbacks and writes active after registry approval is revoked
│   ├── preserves callbacks after registry revocation or registry unavailability
│   ├── stops revoked capabilities only when the owner removes them
│   ├── requires renewed approval for the exact adapter before removed capabilities can be reinstalled
│   ├── forwards arbitrary return bytes and revert bytes exactly
│   ├── rolls back capability writes and ETH receipts on failure
│   └── rejects unknown selectors and nonempty calldata shorter than four bytes
├── multicall
│   ├── atomically replaces capabilities without initializing or erasing module state
│   ├── preserves the external owner for access control and module calls
│   └── restores removals when the replacement is unapproved or collides with a retained module
├── stateful fuzzing
│   └── randomized approvals, additions and removals preserve unique routing and matching enumeration
└── receive
    └── preserves plain ETH funding without an installed capability
